{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Late last week, in a fairly obvious response \nto escalating trade tensions on their southern  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "border, Canada announced that it would be \naccepting an invitation to join the European  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8560,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Union as an associate member, whatever that means. \nBut then just a day later, it was also proposed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that their fellow Commonwealth brothers, Australia \nand New Zealand, could tag along to this party as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well. Now, if these plans do actually go through, \nthey could have massive consequences on global  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trade, global finance, and the global balance \nof power. And on top of just being slightly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "embarrassing to us here in America, it's probably \nonly going to make our own compromised position  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35200,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even more dangerous. But well, there are also a \nlot of unanswered questions. The European Union  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was specifically designed to enable free trade and \nthe free movement of labor between countries in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Europe. So on top of their own internal policies \nwhich could make this team up legally difficult,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are also the very real practical questions \nwhich need to be answered like will Canadians be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56480,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free to work over in Europe like other members are \nand vice versa. Could Canada start using the euro?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And also how is free trade and free movement going \nto work between countries on entirely separate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continents? With a bit of skepticism, there is \nthe reasonable argument that this might not be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more than a run-of-the-mill trade deal \nwith just a slightly different Star Spangled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Banner used for marketing. Also, for what it's \nworth, this is a bigly move which could have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ongoing economic consequences for generations. All \nrealistically being spurred along by aggressive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87360,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trade policy coming from their southern border. \nAnd well, that's fair enough. But this is also a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very long-term solution to a problem that probably \nwon't be around in 2 years time. And reportedly in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98640,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their race to get a fancy sounding headline, these \ntwo groups seem to have forgotten to discuss this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "idea with their own people first. So well, we will \nget to that. As well as what this all means for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108640,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "countries like the UK, who already took the exact \nopposite step just a few years ago. But in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114640,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meantime, right here at home, we should probably \nalso ask if this move means we have successfully  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chased away our most loyal allies for good. Same \nday, the president of the European Commission  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "announced proposals for Canada to be made an \nassociate member of the EU. Roberto Betsah, who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130560,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the president of the European Parliament, has \nsuggested that Australia could follow suit. Why  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should we carry so many countries in Europe? We're \ncarrying the European nations with a $200 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deficit. All we have to do is say, you know what, \nwe're not trading with you anymore. We don't need  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147200,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything they have. Recent data indicates that the \nUK's GDP is approximately 3% lower in 2024 than it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154080,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would have been if the country had remained \nwithin the EU. Okay, so first and foremost,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "associate member of the European Union was up \nuntil recently not actually a real thing. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, if we are being honest, it sounds like \nthe kind of title you give to the CEO's useless  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "child so they feel important without actually \ngiving them any real powers. As it turns out,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174240,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the European Union is actually for countries in \nEurope. Article 49 of the Treaty on European Union  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181040,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lays out how a country joins the EU, and it starts \nwith one requirement. You have to be a European  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186640,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state. And well, as it says right there on their \nlake, Canada is in North America. In addition to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this slight little hiccup, there's also no treaty \narticle or legal framework or definition anywhere  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198320,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in EU law that describes what an associate member \nactually is. So, they kind of made it the up. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be fair, without getting too introspective \nhere, all rules are made up. EU law professor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve Piers has pointed out that this actually \ngives both sides a lot of flexibility because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can innovate both the procedure and content \nof whatever this becomes. This is more of a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "situationship than a real full-blown membership. \nBut again, the title itself doesn't matter nearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as much as what this membership will actually \nentail. So, what is Canada and any other potential  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "new members actually getting out of joining this \nclub? Well, EU membership basically grants or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burdens member states, depending on who you ask, \nwith a few perks and responsibilities. EU members  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can obviously elect representatives to vote on \nEU policy. They have a joint defense pact which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mandates that member states do everything in their \npower to aid any other member if they are attacked  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252800,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by an outside military. And they are part of an \nEU customs union. What this means is that the EU  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "negotiates trade deals as a singular group, which \nobviously gives them much more negotiating power  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as one of the largest collective economies on \nthe planet. It also makes practical sense since  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shipping stuff into and around the European market \nbecomes a lot easier if there is a uniform import  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tax and documentation standards rather than \na different set of rules for each individual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "country, especially since getting to some of those \ncountries means driving through others. However,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282480,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the flip side of this rule, it also means that \nindividual members can't negotiate private deals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the side. So, if France, for example, wanted \nto respond to US tariffs, it would need to do that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as part of the entire EU. But above all, perhaps \nthe biggest defining feature of EU membership is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the four freedoms. The unrestricted movement of \ngoods, services, people, and capital. Basically,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people from member countries can live, work, \ntrade, and move their money into and out of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other member states as if it were their own home. \nSo then what rights and obligations would Canada  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312080,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be getting with its EU light membership plan? \nWell, basically none of these. So it's time to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "learn how many works to find out why what \nlooks like a purely ceremonial gesture is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322240,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "creating so much turmoil back here in America. \nMy sponsor, Cloaked, dared me to see how exposed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328480,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "my information really is. So I put my phone number \nin their site. I was not ready for what came back.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It took a few seconds to pull up my name, my \nold addresses, my relatives, and ID numbers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I never wanted public, which are for sale on data \nbroker sites right now. Data brokers make billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selling your information to spammers, scammers, \nand stalkers, and you technically agreed to it in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some terms and conditions nobody has ever read. \nEvery account you sign up for feeds the machine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they are counting on you never doing anything \nabout it. Most removal services only clean up data  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is already out there. And the problem is \nyou create new exposure with every signup. That  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is what got me used in Cloaked. It finds where \nyour data is being sold and then removes it. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it generates unlimited burner emails, usernames, \nand phone numbers you can call, text, and email  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from inside the app. So, new accounts never tie \nback to your real identity. The next data broker  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sells your file is selling garbage. You are \nthe one playing them now. Cloaked also watches  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the dark web for your leaked information, \nfilters spam calls, comes with an in-built  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "VPN and password manager, and backs it up with a \n$1 million identity theft insurance policy. Go to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cloak.com/hominyworks and enter your phone number \nfor a free security scan. It takes a few seconds,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you will see if your social security number \nis for sale right now. The same link gets you 30%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403920,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off any plan when you are ready to take your data \nback. Okay, so so far Canada's fancy new special  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "EU membership basically grants it none of the \ntypical defining features of being an EU member.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not a great start, but there's actually \neven more to consider here. The first is that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even before this big announcement, Canada already \nhad surprisingly close economic and social ties to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Europe. One really important existing arrangement \nis that Canadians and EU members technically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "already have a system in place to recognize skills \nand qualifications across their borders. But well  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436000,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that agreement has existed for 10 years now and \nin that time only one qualification architecture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has actually been recognized between these groups. \nNow this is a lot different than completely free  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "movement for anybody. But in many ways if they \ncould actually expand this it's kind of the best  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of both worlds especially for Canada. On one hand, \nthey become a highly desirable destination for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "skilled workers where people requiring specific \nlicensing and qualification like doctors, nurses,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and engineers can arrive practically ready \nto work with relatively minimal paperwork.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, they get to pick and choose who \nenters their country, which no matter which side  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the fence you sit on, has still clearly \nbecome a hot issue for regular EU members.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Canada additionally already has agreements in \nplace with the EU regarding things like their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "joint defense fund which as a bit of foreshadowing \nfor later was kind of a way to skirt around an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasingly shaky NATO. Additionally, for a \nlot of rules like the shared customs union,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is obviously a non-starter for Canada \nto even consider because it's a large part  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the reason why they walked away from the \nlatest round of negotiations with America. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Trump administration argued that North America \nshould also negotiate their outward trade deals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collectively as one big group. And for hopefully \nobvious reasons, Canada did not want to be tied  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507120,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to that. We'll make our our decisions about who we \nwant to trade with and how um and uh and including  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on how we work with the United States and other \npartners. Now, it wouldn't be hard to argue that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the European Union's trade policies have been a \nlittle bit more consistent than our own. But even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still, just geographically, it doesn't really make \nmuch sense for them to commit to this. And then on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top of all of this from the EU side, it already \nhas special relationships with countries like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Norway, Iceland, and Switzerland who are not \nmembers or even associate members of the EU,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538080,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but actually have a lot more of these rights than \nCanada will as a member. So, if Canada's new super  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real, totally legit EU membership basically \ngrants it none of the defining characteristics  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of actually being an EU member and both sides \nalready had all of these arguably better deals  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in place. What exactly does this change? Well, \nit's easy to dismiss this as being a complete  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nothing burger as a lot of um uh critics have \nalready pointed out. But the easiest way to tell  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this is still worth paying attention to is \nbecause the American government is collectively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losing its [ __ ] over what they are at the same \ntime calling nothing more than a marketing stunt.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576560,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what the current relationships between \nall the countries involved in this looks like.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's already an overlapping mess of different \ninclusions and exclusions and technicalities.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So drawing another circle really isn't as dumb \nas it sounds as long as both parties are actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "getting something. So there are really four things \nto consider here. The first is that this is a very  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "public commitment to ongoing cooperation. Could \nthe same thing have been achieved with some trade  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deals on top of their already existing bilateral \nagreements? Almost certainly. But actually calling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Canada a member, even if it may be a name only is \na big deal because in theory, it's also going to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be very hard to remove that title. Obviously, this \nmakes for good headlines in the wake of aggressive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trade negotiations leveled by America on both of \nthese groups. But even outside of these latest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619920,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shenanigans, on paper, the relationship does just \nmake good economic sense. The EU needs a source of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy and raw materials, and Canada needs someone \nto sell all of their energy and raw materials,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too. The EU is beefing with Russia, who they used \nto buy all of their energy and raw materials from,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Canada is beefing with America, who they used \nto sell all of their energy and raw materials,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640400,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too. On the surface, this is a pretty sensible \nlittle arrangement. A long-term tangible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "commitment like this, as well as some kind of \nenhanced communications channels will make private  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies a lot more confident making investments \ninto trade across these two markets. I mentioned  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it earlier, but depending on variables like the \nmidterms, court rulings, cholesterol levels,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or 2028, there's a pretty good chance that the \ncurrent trade uncertainty with America won't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continue. So, on the surface, this does seem like \na very extreme long-term move for a problem that's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "probably going to be irrelevant in a few months \ntime. But that's also kind of exactly the point.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Companies from both sides of the pond are kind of \nparalyzed by uncertainty at the moment. They don't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "want to invest into the trade with the US because \nduh. But they also don't want to make significant  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investments into alternatives in case their \nsouthern border just goes back to normal and they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get outco competed by businesses who did nothing. \nIn theory, committing to this long-standing EU  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "membership should tell them that if they commit to \ntrade across the Atlantic, the terms will remain  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consistent and their investments won't be pulled \nout from under them. So, while this associated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "membership may just look like a token gesture, it \nis kind of cementing what is already the best kind  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707440,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of relationship, a relationship of convenience. \nFor example, the second big shakeup is what it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going to mean for the military of both of these \ngroups. There is no requirement for a regular old  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trading partner to develop intermingled military \nhardware. But that's exactly what they are doing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Canada and a good majority of the EU are \nboth part of NATO, the joint procurement fund  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will act as a big pool of money for this group \nspecifically to buy their hardware out of,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which will do a few things. The first is that it \nwill likely exclude American defense contractors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who previously sold a lot of their stuff to Canada \nand the EU. The second is that to replace these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American contractors, this fund is and will likely \ncontinue to lean much more heavily on suppliers in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746640,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the EU and now in Canada and potentially even \nextending that to Australia and New Zealand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depending on how these memberships go. We tend to \nthink of military hardware from American military  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manufacturers as basically irreplaceable. But \nbetween these countries, they now have a huge  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selection of very competent manufacturers. Look, \nI don't want to go full armchair general here,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but just from an economic standpoint, if all \nof these countries start spending their money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on military hardware from each other, they can \nboost their own economies while also cutting off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774640,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lucrative contracts from American companies, who \nalso conveniently, in turn, just so happen to be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of the most vocal lobbyists in Washington. \nAdditionally, defense procurement is arguably  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even more important than any technicalities around \nwhat a membership does or does not mean on paper.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If these countries procure and integrate military \nhardware into their own respective armed forces,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are effectively bound to the hip for as \nlong as that hardware stays in service. Because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798640,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maintaining and resupplying a lot of this stuff \nmeans constant ongoing contracts with the original  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manufacturer. So for example, if Canada purchased \njets from doe, they have committed to a long happy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relationship with France if they want to actually \nkeep them in the air. Now to be fair, we did kind  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of ask for this. One of the chief complaints \nand justifications for America questioning the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818880,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future of NATO as well as pushing these trade \nrelationships was that other member countries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weren't pulling their weight financially. In \na way, we are kind of getting what we want,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but just probably not in the way that we wanted. \nAgain, my insights into actual war fighting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capabilities are effectively meaningless. But \nthe economic point is this is an additional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "major ongoing commitment between an equally \nmajor long-term industrial area of both groups.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The membership itself might be effectively \nmeaningless, but it does solidify what was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "already a serious move to at the very least have \nan alternative to America in a number of important  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fields. So yeah, like a good American, the next \nmost important question is how does all of this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "affect me? The simple answer is it's not great \nand it's probably only going to get worse. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really undermines our already sloppy negotiations \naround the North America free trade deal because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obviously now it's clear that they have other \noptions. This also undermines our negotiating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power with Europe as well because energy was \na big part of the trade with them which was in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn the largest bilateral trade relationship in \nthe world. Another thing this could do is further  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "push these countries away from the US dollar as \na default medium of exchange. The bond market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890320,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is going through all kinds of struggles at the \nmoment. So, it's impossible to say for certain,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but at the very least, it's hard to see how this \ncould be a good thing for the old Benjamins. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899360,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perhaps the most underappreciated potential \noutcome of this new membership could actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be kind of good news. Again, this whole thing was \nonly announced a few days ago, so I don't want to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909200,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get your hopes up yet. But if Canada and maybe \neven Australia and New Zealand become associate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "members of the EU, that could also come with \nmuch closer alignment on their product standards,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially those standards around data privacy, AI \nusage, and the responsible use of technology. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "EU has already one of the strongest forces keeping \nbig tech in line on a lot of these issues. So, if  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these other countries also rolled out enforcement \nin the same way, it would make it a lot harder for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these companies to get around these rules by just \ntreating Europe as its own special little zone.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yeah, despite claiming that we don't really \ncare about all of this, the voices that, let's be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "honest, actually matter in Washington are big mad \nabout what this could mean to their bottom line.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949840,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But well, they aren't the only ones. Another group \nthat wasn't actually thrilled by this announcement  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were a lot of European countries themselves. \nReportedly, a lot of them weren't consulted before  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this invitation was extended, so they were kind \nof blindsided by it. As we have just seen, being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a full EU member comes with a lot of restrictions \nand trade-offs. So the idea of another country  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "joining the club from the outside without agreeing \nto a lot of the same terms was a bit of a blow.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now again, this is a new story, so it's hard to \nsay if any of this will matter. And for what it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worth, Canada already has a good relationship with \nmost of the EU countries anyway. And they would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have supported this move if they were asked. But \nthe fact that they weren't does mean two things.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that the EU is pretty serious about \npushing this relationship. The second is that it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993760,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might not necessarily be off to the best start. \nAnd these slighted member countries may push  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997760,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back against this paper gesture anyway just to \nshow they can. Now, of course, this probably all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could have been avoided if we just left our very \nproductive relationship with Canada alone. But go  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and watch this video next to find out why we are \ndoing all of this to Canada of all countries in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first place. And don't forget to like and \nsubscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
